-- WrathUnleashed MAIN realm: character creation for all 83 race/class pairs (charfix).
-- GENERATED by gen_charfix.py from the realm core's stock world data (mod-playerbots/azerothcore-wotlk 3f2969dd,
-- data/sql/base/db_world), the starting gear and action bars mod-individual-progression (4933d45) puts in this
-- world database, and mod-arac (3f605e0). Applies to acore_world. Safe to run again: every block first removes what
-- this file owns, then writes it. Takes effect when the world server restarts.
--
-- Why: mod-arac has no src/ folder, so AzerothCore's CMake leaves it out of AC_MODULES_LIST and db-import never runs
-- its data/sql/db-world/arac.sql. The 21 pairs that are not stock 3.3.5a therefore have no playercreateinfo row and
-- Player::Create refuses them ("invalid race/class pair", SMSG_CHAR_CREATE = CHAR_CREATE_ERROR).
--
--  1. playercreateinfo: exactly the 83 retail pairs. Stock pairs get their stock row back (undoes any Brawl move to
--     Dalaran); the 21 new pairs get their race's own start (Death Knights are all stock: Acherus).
--  2. charstartoutfit_dbc ids 9001-9042 (overrides CharStartOutfit.dbc): starting gear for the 21 new pairs, both
--     sexes, copied from the same class's outfit of a neighbouring race in this realm's data (weapon, armour,
--     ammo pouch/quiver, food and drink, hearthstone). Stock pairs keep theirs.
--  3. playercreateinfo_action: action bars for the 21 new pairs (the class's buttons, the race's own racials,
--     the outfit's food/drink).
--  4. playercreateinfo_skills: weapon skills the gear donor gets by race (e.g. Guns for a Human Hunter), as rows
--     for exactly the new pair (comment 'charfix ...'). Stock pairs gain nothing.
--  5. skillraceclassinfo_dbc (overrides SkillRaceClassInfo.dbc by ID): mod-arac's rows for the skills the new pairs
--     use, so their class skills (e.g. Marksmanship = Auto Shot) are learnt even if the server's dbc is stock.
--  6. quest_template.AllowableRaces: single-class class quests of a race's own faction (pet taming, totems, warlock
--     demons, druid forms) also allow the races that only have that class as a new pair. Stock pairs see no change.
--     The original values are kept in ov_charfix_quest_races so this block can always be redone from them.
-- Nothing here touches characters, accounts, or any row of a stock pair except putting playercreateinfo back to stock.

